---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Thriai — Fractional CFO + AI-native finance platform for tech companies">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Fractional CFO · AI Finance Platform · Revenue Systems</div>
      <h1>Finance leadership that ships with its own data platform.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Thriai is a fractional CFO firm for technology companies. Every client runs on a governed, AI-queryable finance stack, delivered by the same senior person who owns your numbers. No junior bench, no month-old templated reporting, no call-us pricing.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Book a 30-minute call</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/pricing">See published pricing</a>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-row">
        <div><b>Business day 5</b>Close and reporting SLA</div>
        <div><b>60+ checks</b>Automated tie-outs every month</div>
        <div><b>Senior only</b>The person you hire does the work</div>
        <div><b>Published</b>Pricing you can read before we talk</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="services">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">What we do</div>
      <h2>Three practices, one platform, one relationship.</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:64ch">Incumbent fractional CFO firms sell people. AI consultancies sell tools. Thriai sells both, from one team that has closed the month, survived diligence, and built production finance infrastructure.</p>
      <div class="grid c3" style="margin-top:34px">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag hot">Core</span>
          <h3>Fractional CFO</h3>
          <p class="muted">Owned monthly close, 13-week cash, budget vs. actual, board packages, ARR and SaaS KPI reporting, rolling forecast, fundraise and diligence support, pricing and comp design.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Retainers from $3.5K/mo</li>
            <li>Pre-seed through PE-backed</li>
            <li>Bookkeeping runs inside the QA-gated pipeline</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag hot">Differentiator</span>
          <h3>AI Finance Platform</h3>
          <p class="muted">A governed warehouse, an ARR and KPI semantic layer, automated reporting, and AI access with guardrails. Built once from a proven template, tuned to your stack, yours to keep.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Finance AI Assessment in 2 to 3 weeks</li>
            <li>Platform build in 6 to 10 weeks</li>
            <li>Agents for close prep, reporting, collections</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="tag">Practice area</span>
          <h3>Revenue Systems</h3>
          <p class="muted">Quote-to-cash integrity, CRM and CPQ architecture, and GTM data that ties to the general ledger. Findings quantified in dollars, not slide decks.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Quote-to-Cash Audit</li>
            <li>ARR Data Quality Rebuild</li>
            <li>BI stack with tie-out tests</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Why it works</div>
      <h2>Built the way finance should have been built all along.</h2>
      <div class="grid c2" style="margin-top:30px">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>What buyers complain about</th><th>What Thriai does instead</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Senior sells, junior delivers</td><td><b>Senior-only delivery.</b> AI leverage replaces the junior bench.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Month-old templated reporting</td><td><b>Business-day-5 close</b> and live governed dashboards.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ten-day closes, three-month onboardings</td><td><b>Template-repo onboarding</b> measured in days.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>No help with systems</td><td><b>Revenue Systems practice</b> built in, not referred out.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Opaque call-us pricing</td><td><b>Published tiers.</b> Most competitors hide theirs.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>AI pilots that die</td><td><b>Data foundation first.</b> Semantic layer and QA gates before any agent.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div>
          <h3>How an engagement runs</h3>
          <div class="grid steps" style="gap:26px;margin-top:22px">
            <div class="card"><b>Assess.</b> <span class="muted">Two to three weeks mapping your finance stack, data quality, and the highest-ROI automation candidates. You get a roadmap either way.</span></div>
            <div class="card"><b>Build.</b> <span class="muted">Your client repo is cloned from a proven template: ingest from your books, payroll, billing, and CRM into a governed model with penny tie-outs.</span></div>
            <div class="card"><b>Run.</b> <span class="muted">Monthly close, reporting, forecast, and board work on a retainer, with agents doing production and a human doing judgment.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Who it is for</div>
      <h2>Technology companies between first revenue and first full-time CFO.</h2>
      <div class="grid c3" style="margin-top:30px">
        <div class="card"><h3>VC-backed SaaS, pre-seed to Series A</h3><p class="muted">$1M to $15M revenue. You need investor-grade numbers and a real close before you can afford a CFO. Foundation and Operate tiers, plus fundraise projects.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>PE-backed tech, $10M to $100M</h3><p class="muted">Sponsor reporting, ARR that ties, quote-to-cash that stops leaking. Strategic CFO, platform build, and the Quote-to-Cash Audit.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>PE sponsors and operating partners</h3><p class="muted">One relationship, many deployments. A standardized assessment across portfolio companies, then a repeatable finance data layer per company.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt tight">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center">
      <h2>Start with a conversation, not a proposal.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Thirty minutes. We will tell you whether the fit is real and what it would cost, in that order.</p>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Book a call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
